Z||000000||bHooper||12-15-2000||01:03 PM||||i just picked up my GT from the alignment shop... <B>WoW!</B>  She is tight!<P>i am going to have to be carefull, or i am going to kill myself in this thing, now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>for those that don't know, i have totally rebuilt the suspension, except for the half shafts, rear tranny mount, engine mounts and front swaybar, everything is new.<P>i cant imagine haveing the car any lower.  amazing ride.<P>the alignment shop dialed in -1 camber at all wheels, so it is twitchy...  speaking of which...<P>i noticed that the rear tends to feel every swerve in the asphalt.  is that to be expected with what i have done?  travis???<P>next up... new mounts and tires!  but first, i must pay this off.<P>smiling all the way...<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||12-15-2000||01:08 PM||||After I lowered my car I had a set of 235/60R14's on it. The car was kinda twitchy due to the higher sidewalls. I switched to 225/50R15's (BFG Euro T/A's) and the twitchyness (if that is a word)went away. With the tighter suspension you need a tire with lower profile and strong sidewall's.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||12-15-2000||01:34 PM||||Congrats, Brian!  Any idea what tire brand you're going with?||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||12-15-2000||02:05 PM||||no plans on the tires, yet.  i really don't have much cash, at the moment.  my cherokee needs tires, and brakes, also.<P>as for the sidewall thing, that does make sense. i am running 215/65/15's in the rear (used tires i bought for cheap), and 205/60/15's in the front.<P>however, b4 the suspension job, i had noticed a wiggle in the rear... on the same road.<P>would poor tranny seals cause this?  how bout engine mounts?<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||12-15-2000||04:53 PM||||Brian, great news!! I know you are happy to be driving your Fiero again and I'm happy that I could play a small part in that.<P>Just to let you know, we will be working on the anti-bump steer kits next week, gonna put one on my car and see how it performs before offering it to the public but, it sounds like the kit would take the "twitch" out of the rear of yours........i'll keep ya posted if you are interested....||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||12-15-2000||05:05 PM||||Old tires act very differnet from new ones, and  Like Oreif said the sidewall makes a big difference. I noticed a <B>huge</B> difference between new and old tires when I replaced them on my Formula. With my old tires the sidewalls were really 'tired', and wandered all over the road, following every little rut(even invisible ones) in the asphault. After I put new tires on, it was a new car. Steering was much lighter, the car tracked straight always, took bumps better, and the heandling was much improved. I had reaplaced the old tires with the same brand and model, so it was just the difference between old and new, not different design.<P>Spelling mistakes are because my hands are shaking from being cold working out in the garage.<P>I know you put poly everywhere, you did replace the cradle bushings while you were in there, right? If not, the old factory rubber could be causing the reat end liveliness.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||12-15-2000||07:23 PM||||Hoop:<P>I look forward to riding in it after all the work.  It will be interesting to compare the before and after feel of the car.<P>Look forward to seeing it on it's wheels tomorrow!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||12-18-2000||08:57 AM||||i replaced all the bushings with poly.  the only things that i didn't replace on the suspension were the front swaybar,  and the rear inner tie rod ends.<P>it is possible that the "sway" is also coming from the tie rods, or the tires.  the rears aren't all that old.  i put a little air in them this morning and it seemed to help, a bit... i will let you know more, later.<P>hoop||||reg||2
